A||||12||2xsess||Digital Camera memory chips||||8||
Z||000000||2xsess||12-27-2000||09:09 PM||||Why is it that the stupid little memory chip thing costs almost as much as the camera?<P>I got a Kodak digital Camera for Christmas and when I went to get one of the chips I almost fell over when I saw that a 48MB one was $120. The cheapest one was $50. <P>I just don't get it. Thanks, I had to vent a little.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||8
Z||000001||Old Lar||12-27-2000||09:28 PM||||Hey, Kodak has to make money somehow since you are not buying film.  I did get a 64 mb card for $128 tax included.  With my Kodak 280 zoom camera (2 million pixel resolution) the 64 mb chip holds 104 images using the highest resolution. SanDisk also makes a compatible CompactFlash memory card.  Shop around, you may get a better price.  You'll never have to buy film or processing again.<P>I love the camera and the photos it takes.  Tweaking the images on the cmputer takes some getting used to, but its lots of fun.<P>BTW, I've worked at Kodak for over 30 years.  I don't get any price break either.||||reg||3
Z||000002||Cooter||12-27-2000||09:56 PM||||I like the memory cards that work with the USB reader- very fast transfers compared to using the camera hooked up to the mouse port. I have a PCMCIA card reader for a computer that works great for reading the pics but my new PC only has PCI slots and the controller card is an ISA. (Also makes file transfers from desktop to laptop pretty easy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )||||reg||1
Z||000003||sqoach||12-27-2000||10:29 PM||||if you're not gonna be taking a lot of pictures at one time until you make it to your computer, i wouldn't bother with a high MB chip/card thingy. i think, but not sure, our's is a 8MB chip and it holds like 45 pictures at the highest resolution.<BR>just my 2 1/2 cents<P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mysig_2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||LarryB||12-27-2000||11:04 PM||||If your 8MB chip holds 45 pictures at the highest resolution then your camera's "high-res" setting must be like 640x480 or the specific jpeg algorithm your camera uses must be pretty lossy. <P>I have a 48MB card in my camera (Nikon Coolpix 900) and at high res the camera reports it will hold around 74 pictures.  I know from experience that with this camera a high-res pic will usually average between 500-600Kb/picture. T<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||2xsess||12-28-2000||01:43 AM||||High res on mine is 1152x864 or something like that. <P>I think for right now I'll stick with the internal memory. The only time I'll be taking more than 18 pics would be at shows and my schedule doesn't appear to allow me to make any shows until spring of 2002  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||onfire||12-28-2000||02:48 AM||||You should see the memory cards for the mp3 player in my truck $99.99 for 32 mb at Comp USA (the only place I can find them).I think they're about 69 or 79 dollars if I get them off the net. shipping not included.<P>------------------<BR>"I seen it on the internet, and I believe everthing on the net."<BR><A HREF="http://homestead.deja.com/user.on_fire/on_fire.html" TARGET=_blank>Check out my waist of banbwidth.</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||vietnow||12-28-2000||03:56 AM||||its just RAM.. its expensive for computers too...<P><P>------------------<BR>Vietnow --<BR>1986 Celica GTS||||reg||1
Z||000008||Robert||12-28-2000||10:46 AM||||You might want to check out Ebay.  There are people selling the cards for much less than the store.  I bought my camera on Ebay, and have had no problems.||||reg||1
Z||000009||onfire||12-28-2000||01:59 PM||||Ram is getting cheaper  pc's 256mb pc133 for $115 not to far from my house. <A HREF="http://www.infotechnow.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.infotechnow.com/</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||rogergarrison||12-28-2000||05:31 PM||||I just bought myself a Panasonic digital camera, i made sure I got one that records photos on a reg 3 1/2'' floppy disk. It also uses superdisks, can store 1500 (yes fifteen hundred) pics on one disk. I can just take the disk out of my camera and put in my disk drive to view, print or mail.||||reg||1
